<title>NETHERLANDS: AKZO NOBEL TO COMPLETE SALT SALE IN Q2.</title>
<headline>AKZO NOBEL TO COMPLETE SALT SALE IN Q2.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said on Friday it expected to complete the sell-off of its Salt America activities in the second quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The divestment of the Salt America activities to Cargil Inc. will be completed in the second quarter,&quot; Akzo said in a statement accompanying its first quarter results.</p>
<p>Akzo reported first-quarter net profit rose to 340 million guilders from a year-earlier 332 million.</p>
<p>Akzo sold its Pennsylvania-based de-icing business to commodities giant Cargill last August after earlier closing down its Retsof salt mine.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
